  "brief_md": "# Evidence Brief — P02: Privacy-Preserving Proof-of-Human Verification Layer\n\n## Idea as written\nA privacy-preserving verification layer proving a person in a call, message, transaction, or review is human — sold to banks, marketplaces, dating apps, and video-call platforms.\n\n## Payer\nThe platform pays, not the end user — every identified competitor monetizes the business, not the verified human. **Price hypothesis:** usage-tiered SaaS starting near $9.99–$249/month for self-serve customers (not.bot: https://not.bot/verify/), scaling to enterprise contracts of $500–$2,000/month for banks to avoid procurement escalation (https://prospeo.io/s/selling-to-banks).\n\n## Competitors\n- **not.bot** — $9.99/mo (Sandbox, 10 MAU) up to $249/mo (Basic, 1,000 MAU) + per-MAU overage, open-source SDK, self-hosted. https://not.bot/verify/\n- **useHUMA** — Free tier (1,000 verifications/mo) through $499/mo Enterprise, explicitly includes 'Agent Shield · AI agent detection'. https://humaverify.com/pricing\n- **World ID / World.org** — no public per-call price; floated protocol fee model (~$0.40/user/month) and has already landed Zoom as an enterprise partner for live deepfake verification. https://world.org/blog/announcements/world-id-fees-the-revenue-potential-from-world-id ; https://www.techfinitive.com/zoom-partners-with-tools-for-humanity-to-provide-real-time-verification-against-deepfake-videos/\n- **Incognia** — enterprise 'Physical Presence Score' product, claims 1B+ devices in network, no public pricing. https://www.linkedin.com/posts/andreferraz_proving-youre-human-shouldnt-require-an-activity-7447043500652810240-uBFC\n- **POY Verify** — private beta, waitlist only, no public pricing. https://poyverify.com/docs\n\n## Acquisition channels\n1. **Self-serve developer/API launch** (Product Hunt + directories): $0–$2,000, realistically $200–$500 for an indie founder. https://autosaaslaunch.com/blog/product-hunt-launch-cost-breakdown\n2. **Direct bank sales**: 6–18 month cycle, SOC 2 Type II required before outbound, entry pricing capped at $500–$2K/mo to avoid procurement escalation. https://prospeo.io/s/selling-to-banks\n\n## Demand evidence\n- \"It's always hard for me to believe I sent a bot money when obviously it was a scam\" — r/OnlineDating user. https://www.reddit.com/r/OnlineDating/comments/103uuzh/how_do_you_recognize_fake_profiles_and_bots/\n- \"As AI continues to blur the line between real and synthetic, establishing trust online becomes essential\" — Trevor Traina, Chief Business Officer, Tools for Humanity, on the Zoom/World ID partnership. https://www.techfinitive.com/zoom-partners-with-tools-for-humanity-to-provide-real-time-verification-against-deepfake-videos/\n- CFO authorized a $243,000 wire after being fooled by an AI-cloned voice deepfake. https://www.usbank.com/corporate-and-commercial-banking/insights/risk/mitigation/ai-deepfake-fraud.html\n\n## Case for\nOpen-source cryptographic and liveness primitives mean a solo founder with AI coding agents can assemble a credible verification API in weeks. The pain is well documented across all four named segments (bot dating profiles, deepfake bank wires, Zoom deepfake impersonation). A usage-based price matching not.bot/useHUMA lets one person reach small marketplaces/dating apps/review sites via a near-zero-cost Product Hunt-style launch, without needing a sales team.\n\n## Case against\nThe named enterprise customers are already served: Zoom has integrated World ID's Deep Face product; Incognia already has 1B+ devices and enterprise partners; World ID has an Orb hardware network and protocol-fee roadmap. Banks require 6–18 month sales cycles and SOC 2/ISO 27001 before any serious conversation — incompatible with a six-week build. The reachable self-serve segment already has at least four free-tier direct competitors, pushing pricing toward zero. 'Privacy-preserving' design does not exempt the product from biometric-privacy regulatory risk — Worldcoin's